course: dictionary
lesson: 2730
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around the word. This is its context. «Being diplomatic» means not saying what you really think, to avoid hurting or angering someone.
explain: Here the clues are «not saying what you really think» and «avoid hurting». So diplomatic means careful and polite, saying things in a way that does not upset people. Ask yourself: does this meaning fit the sentence?
explain: In history lessons the word means something else. Diplomatic talks are talks between countries, and diplomatic relations are the friendly links between them. Here diplomatic is about diplomats, the people who work for their country in other countries.
fact: Diplomatic can mean to do with diplomats: people who work for their country in other countries and help countries talk to each other.
fact: Diplomatic can also mean careful and polite, saying things in a way that does not upset people.
fact: «Being diplomatic» means not saying what you really think, to avoid hurting or angering someone.
fact: Diplomatic talks, diplomatic relations and diplomatic answers are phrases you may meet in history and everyday life.
fact: Diplomatic is an adjective. Its forms are diplomatic, more diplomatic and most diplomatic.
exercise: «Being diplomatic» means not saying what you really think, to avoid hurting or angering someone. What does diplomatic mean here? | Happy and silly | Tired and slow | *Careful and polite, so no one is upset | Loud and rude
exercise: In history lessons, diplomatic talks are held between countries. What does diplomatic mean in this phrase? | To do with sports teams | *To do with diplomats, the people who work for their country abroad | To do with cooking food | Very short and quick
exercise: Which word means the same as careful and polite, so people are not upset? | noisy | *diplomatic | blunt | gloomy
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you the adjective form that means most careful. | talks | relations | *most diplomatic | diplomatic
test: Lily says her friend's drawing is messy, but she is diplomatic and praises the colours first. What does diplomatic mean in this sentence? | Rude and blunt | Very quiet and shy | Happy and loud | *Careful and polite, so the friend is not upset
test: The two countries began diplomatic relations after the war. Which meaning fits? | Very fast at running | Careful not to upset people at a party | Cold and wet | *To do with diplomats and the links between countries
exam: Jayden must tell his grandad that his soup is too salty, so he chooses a diplomatic way to say it. Which is the best meaning of diplomatic here? | Working for another country | Quiet and sad | *Careful and polite, saying things so the person is not upset | Shouting loudly at the table
